                    <death when="1810-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>merchant</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Christopher Alderson was a merchant of Lawrence Lane in 8 November 1782,
                            proposed 8 November 1782 by Joseph Brown of Gracechurch Street, and
                            seconded by Richard Sharp of Fish Street Hill. In 1766, he became a
                            partner of John Story, warehouseman, Lawrence Lane. He was an East India
                            merchant in Lawrence Lane in 1789. By 6 October 1792 he was on the
                            Hackney Committee for the Association to Defend Liberty and Property
                            against Republicans and Levellers (Oracle 7 October 1792). He was buried
                            31 December 1810, St John Hackney, age 85. His will, PCC 1811, indicates
                            that he lived in Homerton. His probable birthplace is Askrigg,
                            Yorkshire; one of his executors was John Pearson of Lawrence Lane,
                            warehouseman. </p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>

